BANNED_PHRASES = [
    "delve", "leverage", "tapestry", "unlock", "harness", "realm", "robust",
    "pivotal", "seamless", "foster", "underscore", "elevate", "cutting-edge",
    "game-changer", "paradigm", "holistic", "synergy", "groundbreaking",
    "revolutionize", "meticulous", "in today's fast-paced world",
    "it's important to note", "it's worth noting", "not just X, but Y",
    "in conclusion", "at the end of the day", "embark on a journey",
    "navigate the complexities", "unprecedented",
]

HUMANIZING_GUIDELINES = """Write like a specific person with an actual point of view, not a neutral summary. ALWAYS contract -- never write "do not" (write "don't"), "is not" ("isn't"), "does not" ("doesn't"), "cannot" ("can't"), "will not" ("won't"), "you are" ("you're"), "it is" ("it's"), "that is" ("that's"), "she is" ("she's"), "he is" ("he's"). Uncontracted forms are one of the strongest signals of stiff, robotic-sounding narration -- treat them as errors, not stylistic choices. Vary sentence structure so paragraphs don't all follow the same topic-then-explanation-then-example shape. State things plainly instead of hedging everything. Prefer concrete, specific details over vague claims. Never use the banned words/phrases listed separately -- they are recognizable AI tells that readers now spot immediately."""

PACING_EXAMPLE = """Write with the kind of rhythmic sentence-length variety Gary Provost is well known for teaching -- short, punchy sentences mixed deliberately with longer, flowing ones, so the ear never settles into a monotonous drone. Draw on your own knowledge of that rhythmic style; do not reproduce his actual published text.

Here is an original demonstration of that same rhythm (write in this style -- do not reuse this exact wording or topic, it's a rhythm demonstration only):

"Attraction is not a switch. It's a sequence. You meet someone, you feel something, and you assume that feeling is the whole story -- but it almost never is. Beneath every spark sits a slower, quieter process running in the background, deciding, without asking your permission, whether tonight becomes something more than a nice memory." """
